# Line endings are frozen exactly as committed.
#
# SOURCE_INTEGRITY.txt, SOURCE_INTEGRITY_V11.txt and SOURCE_INTEGRITY_V12.txt
# record SHA-256 over raw file bytes, and scripts/static_audit_v12.py verifies
# them. Any line-ending translation between commit and checkout changes those
# bytes and breaks every one of those hashes on a platform whose convention
# differs from the one the file was written on.
#
# `-text` tells git to treat every path as binary for this purpose: store what
# it is given, hand back exactly the same bytes. This is a correctness
# requirement here, not a style preference.
* -text
